.TH BIGINTSHIFTLEFT 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntShiftLeft, bigIntShiftRight, bigIntGetBit \- shift or inspect bits of a big integer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigIntShiftLeft(BigInt *" "a" ", int " "bits" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigIntShiftRight(BigInt *" "a" ", int " "bits" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigIntGetBit(const BigInt *" "a" ", int " "bit_index" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The shift functions modify a in place by bits binary positions.
Left shift multiplies by a power of two; right shift discards low bits.
Right shifting past all active limbs produces canonical zero.
A zero count has no effect; a negative count delegates to the opposite shift.
.PP
.B bigIntGetBit()
returns the bit at bit_index, counting from zero at the least significant bit.
The index must be nonnegative.  Indices beyond the active limbs return zero.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Left shift returns 0 or INT_MAX for capacity overflow.
Right shift returns 0 for nonnegative counts; negative counts can return
the delegated left-shift error.
Bit lookup returns 0 or 1.
.SH BUGS
Left shift conservatively reserves an extra limb and can reject a shift
whose actual result would fit.
Do not pass INT_MIN as a shift count, or counts large enough to overflow
intermediate signed arithmetic.  Negative bit indices are not validated.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
